                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "53d8f570-e28e-35d3-b179-d86aeb112cef",
                        "entry_id": "1c3425e0-eb61-3031-be4e-74d741845f3c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To give new life, energy or encouragement (to); to refresh, enliven."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "808c56d0-a882-484d-9cb7-7672ec916c85",
                                "sense_id": "53d8f570-e28e-35d3-b179-d86aeb112cef",
                                "text": "Painters, when they work on white grounds, place before them colours mixed with blue and green, to recreate their eyes, white wearying […] the sight more than any."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "157d6449-6902-4c2e-9863-884d8cbd53ef",
                                "sense_id": "53d8f570-e28e-35d3-b179-d86aeb112cef",
                                "text": "These ripe fruit[…] recreate the nostrils with their aromatick scent."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a4ac9409-418d-49c4-af7a-32fa303fc633",
                                "sense_id": "53d8f570-e28e-35d3-b179-d86aeb112cef",
                                "text": "Odoraments to smell to, of rose-water, violet flowers, balm, rose-cakes, vinegar, etc., do much recreate the brains and spirits […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "23bdc264-4e86-3ccd-be78-388b5693cdee",
                        "entry_id": "1c3425e0-eb61-3031-be4e-74d741845f3c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To enjoy or entertain oneself."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "reflexive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3715a7d0-b2ff-4fa8-a724-b55620904d3e",
                                "sense_id": "23bdc264-4e86-3ccd-be78-388b5693cdee",
                                "text": "In Italy, though they bide in cities in winter, which is more gentlemanlike, all the summer they come abroad to their country-houses, to recreate themselves."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "32600434-7734-4c95-a7a6-28bb99a59edb",
                                "sense_id": "23bdc264-4e86-3ccd-be78-388b5693cdee",
                                "text": "St. John, who recreated himself with sporting with a tame partridge"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e69cc7a1-2376-3d8f-bb87-065b99e92151",
                        "entry_id": "1c3425e0-eb61-3031-be4e-74d741845f3c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To take recreation."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8289dd6c-f883-40aa-abc7-0e08c409be0b",
                                "sense_id": "e69cc7a1-2376-3d8f-bb87-065b99e92151",
                                "text": "Phonecams are proliferating like mad, their tiny eyes fuzzily probing so many corners of public and private life that they have begun to alter how people communicate and recreate."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
